      "rationale": "The specification declares the country of origin for both the product and its primary ingredient (chicken stock, 52%) as France. Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011 Art. 26(3) requires that if the origin of the food is given and it differs from the primary ingredient, this must be stated. Here, both are the same (France), so no additional statement is required. There is no evidence that omitting the origin would mislead the consumer, and the relevant information is provided.",
